Ads in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-maps/">Apple Maps</a> are live in the United States and Canada, which means iPhone and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> users will see them when searching for locations and when viewing Suggested Places.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/apple-maps-ads-live.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1061108" /><br/>
Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/24/apple-maps-ads-announced/">announced plans</a> to bring ads to the Maps app in March, and said the feature would roll out starting in late summer. Apple confirmed to <em><a href="https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/25/apple-maps-launches-ads-on-iphone-heres-whats-new/">9to5Mac</a></em> that ads began showing up for users over the last few days, with ad placement to ramp up in the coming weeks.<br/>
<br/>
Ads are shown in Suggested Places when initiating a search and after searching if a company has bought an ad for a keyword you're looking for. Ads are shown at the top of search results, with one ad per set of search results.<br/>
<br/>
There is no option to turn off ads in the Maps app, but ads are clearly labeled with a blue "Ad" tag. Apple says ads you interact with in the Maps app are not associated with your Apple Account, and data is not shared with third parties.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has been preparing to launch ads all summer, with signs of ads <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/13/apple-maps-app-ads-summer-2026/">showing up</a> in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a> updates. Apple started allowing businesses to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/14/ads-coming-soon-to-apple-maps/">purchase ad slots</a> in August, offering a 15 percent credit toward future ad spend as an incentive.<br/>
<br/>
Ads for home services, bail bonds, and cryptocurrency ATMs are not allowed in the Maps app per <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/15/apple-maps-ad-prohibitied-categories/">Apple's Advertising Services policy</a>. Ads that promote or reference medical services may be allowed, and are evaluated on a case-by-case basis. Maps ads also have to adhere to Apple's other advertising rules.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-ads/">Apple Ads</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-maps/">Apple Maps</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-maps-ads-live/">Apple Maps Ads Are Here, and There&#039;s No Way to Turn Them Off</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apple-maps-ads-are-here-and-theres-no-way-to-turn-them-off.2487948/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>